// THE STORE PRICE PRESET (2026-10-12; owner: "set pricing for materials one
// time, preset from Home Depot — go through") — pure data.
//
// Home Depot's listed prices for the deck's materials, surveyed ONCE from the
// listings search engines index (homedepot.com itself was not read — it
// refuses automated requests), each converted to the unit its price-book row
// is priced in (a 16-ft board's price ÷ 16 for a foot of lumber; a bundle ×
// 3 for a square of shingles; a box ÷ its count for one screw). They replace
// the example default where Home Depot sells the item; what it does not sell
// (exotic hardwoods, trusses, a steel ring plate) and labor stay examples.
// Like an example, a store price is scaled to the job's market and gives way
// to the shop's own number, typed once in Your prices. It is a snapshot: the
// date says how old it is.

